<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia March producer output prices falls.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia March producer output prices falls.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's manufacturing output prices fell 0.1 percent in March to be 0.7 percent up on the year, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>Prices rose 0.2 percent in February for a 0.6 percent year-on-year rise.  </p>
<p>Manufacturing output prices (base 1988/89):</p>
<p>				    Index   mth/mth pct  yr/yr pct</p>
<p>    March			 122.2     -0.1	 +0.7</p>
<p>    February		    122.3     +0.2	 +0.6</p>
<p>    March 1996		  121.4     -0.2	 +1.7</p>
<p>Note - The bureau said price decreases for motor vehicles and refined petroleum products were the main contributors to the fall in the index.</p>
<p>It said the fall in March manufacturing output prices was the first fall since June 1996.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
